# CODEOWNERS — second-party review on the paths that define what is POSSIBLE
#
# Aaron 2026-08-10: "do both, codeowners first" — the fast half of k-of-n on
# discriminated-union / workflow changes. The Zeta-native half (signed change
# attestations verified by `MultiSignatureVerification`, trusting no third party) follows;
# this is the bounded overlap, not the destination.
#
# ## Why these paths and not more
#
# The argument is not "important files need review". It is narrower: a discriminated union
# or a workflow defines **the set of actions that exist**. Injecting a new action is the
# attack; widening the action space is the same attack one level up. Everything listed below
# either enumerates what may happen or decides who may make it happen.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed: ordinary implementation, docs, research, workitems. Requiring a
# second party on those would grind the autonomous loop to a halt for no security gain, and
# a control that makes normal work painful is a control people route around.
#
# ## What this actually buys, and its limit
#
# Every agent in this repo commits as `AceHack`. GitHub forbids approving your own pull
# request, so an agent-authored change to a path below cannot be self-approved — it needs
# `maximdolphin` or `Addisons820`. That is a real second party, not a formality.
#
# **The limit, stated plainly:** this trusts GitHub as the authority on who consented. GitHub
# can be compelled, can be wrong, and is a hub — precisely the shape the substrate refuses
# everywhere else. That is why it is the first half and not the whole answer.
#
# ## This file requires a second party to change
#
# `/.github/CODEOWNERS` is listed below and owns itself. A control that can be edited away by
# the party it constrains is not a control.
#
# NOTE: CODEOWNERS alone does nothing. It takes effect only when branch protection on `main`
# has **"Require review from Code Owners"** enabled (currently
# `required_approving_review_count: none`). That is a repository-settings change and belongs
# to a human.

# ── The control itself ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/.github/CODEOWNERS                        @maximdolphin @Addisons820

# ── CI gates: changing a gate changes what may reach main ─────────────────────
/.github/workflows/                        @maximdolphin @Addisons820

# ── Action-space definitions: the DUs that enumerate what can happen ──────────
/src/Core/DerivationProtocol.fs            @maximdolphin @Addisons820
/src/Core/MultiSignatureVerification.fs    @maximdolphin @Addisons820

# ── Authorization: the consent gate and its emergency bypass ──────────────────
/src/Core/Consent/                         @maximdolphin @Addisons820

# ── The rules that govern how every agent works ───────────────────────────────
/.claude/rules/                            @maximdolphin @Addisons820
/docs/governance/                          @maximdolphin @Addisons820
